  "severity": "important",
  "description": "A flaw was found in util-linux's mount(8). When an external mount helper exits with an error, the post-mount hooks (X-mount.idmap, X-mount.owner, X-mount.group, X-mount.mode) still run as if the mount had succeeded, so a local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized entry can run privileged operations on the pre-existing target filesystem and escalate privileges.",
